# TODO - Reusable block catalogue

## Objective

Build a deterministic catalogue of verified arithmetic, branch, memory, calling
convention, and runtime blocks so common operations are solved once and reused
instead of synthesized from scratch for every compilation. Every reusable block
must expose the state and layout contract required for safe linking.

## Acceptance

- Every catalog entry binds semantic pre/postconditions, entry/exit machine
  state,
  target profile, layout assumptions, mutation footprint, cost metrics,
  provenance, and verifier identity.
- Lookup never substitutes a block whose complete composition contract does not
  match the requested operation and current linker assumptions.
- Catalogue entries are independently verifiable and reproducible under
  the available CPU search backend. CUDA-produced entries use the *same*
  semantic/profile/link/verifier identity when P8 supports them; live CUDA
  or identical GPU/CPU artifact bytes are not P6 catalogue prerequisites.
- A CPU/reference path remains sufficient for correctness, and accelerator
  failure/unavailability changes performance rather than semantic acceptance.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.
- **Finite acceptance witness:** One verified reusable entry in each of five
  declared categories (arithmetic, branch, memory, call and I/O/runtime), one
  invalid composition rejection and one repeated CPU lookup; GPU rows are P8
  follow-up.

## 282-Phase Micro-Operation Catalogue Candidate

If P2/P4 independently admit a 282-position structural-phase block, store it
as a **conditional, verified micro-operation**, not as a globally portable
282-cell opcode template. Distinguish the arithmetic / branch / memory /
call / I/O semantic role from the selected physical placement.

- Record canonical profile and source/loader identity, 282-phase class,
  actual source length and address, register/memory/input preconditions,
  state/encryption mutation footprint, output, exit/continuation contract,
  step/search cost and verifier receipt. Return to an identical address
  must additionally show that the next entry satisfies all modified-memory
  requirements.
- For a finite repeated-lookup trial, compare one identical placement with
  one shifted-by-282 candidate and one deliberately mutated-memory case;
  accept reuse only when the **complete** contract matches. Phase equality
  without state equality must reject.
- Treat a fixed 282-cell envelope as an optional search family; allow other
  code lengths if required for correctness. Neither exhaustive exploration
  of 14,348,907 addresses nor the unbounded cycle claim is required by P6.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `accelerator/`, `algorithms/`,
  `optimizer/`,
  `benchmarks/accelerator/`, `tests/optimizer/`.
- Required evidence: block manifests, verifier results, deterministic catalogue
  identity, link compatibility fixtures, and cross-backend differential tests.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `deterministic-cpu-optimizer`,
  `translation-validation`, `malbolge-layout-and-encoding-backend`,
  `state-aware-malbolge-linker`.
